<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of African</p>
<p>Nations Cup qualifying matches played at the weekend:</p>
<p>Group One:</p>
<p>In Harare:</p>
<p>Zimbabwe 1 Angola 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Goalscorer: Wilfred Mugeyi (31st min penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>    Standings   P  W  D  L  F  A Pts </p>
<p>    Ghana	 2  1  1  0  2  1  4</p>
<p>    Zimbabwe    2  1  1  0  1  0  4</p>
<p>    Angola	2  0  0  2  1  3  0</p>
<p>Next match:</p>
<p>Angola v Ghana, Luanda, June 22</p>
<p>Group Two:</p>
<p>In Cotonou:</p>
<p>Benin 1 Algeria 1 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Benin: Moussa Latoundji (35th)</p>
<p>Algeria: Abdelhafid Tasfaout (51st)</p>
<p>In Bamako:</p>
<p>Mali 1 Ivory Coast 2 (halftime 1-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Mali - Modibo Sidibe (14th)</p>
<p>Ivory Coast - Ibrahim Bakayoko (13th), Joel Tiehi (22nd)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Mali	  3  2  0  1  4  3  6</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast 3  2  0  1  4  5  6</p>
<p>    Algeria     3  1  1  1  5  3  4</p>
<p>    Benin	 3  0  1  2  2  4  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast v Algeria, Abidjan, June 22</p>
<p>Mali v Benin, Bamako, June 22</p>
<p>Group Three:</p>
<p>In Addis Ababa:</p>
<p>Ethiopia 1 Egypt 1 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ethiopia: Aseyed Tesfaye (58th min)</p>
<p>Egypt: Akram Abdelmajid (71st min)</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000</p>
<p>In Dakar:</p>
<p>Senegal 0 Morocco 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Senegal   3  1  2  0  2  1  5</p>
<p>    Egypt     3  0  3  0  2  2  3</p>
<p>    Morocco   2  0  2  0  1  1  2</p>
<p>    Ethiopia  2  0  1  1  2  3  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Senegal v Ethiopia, Dakar, June 21</p>
<p>Morocco v Egypt, Casablanca, June 22</p>
<p>Group Four:</p>
<p>In Conakry:</p>
<p>Guinea 1 Sierra Leone 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Fode Camara (67th min)</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Guinea	 1  1  0  0  1  0  3</p>
<p>    Tunisia	2  1  0  1  2  1  3</p>
<p>    Sierra Leone 1  0  0  1  0  2  0</p>
<p>Next match:</p>
<p>Sierra Leone v Tunisia, Freetown, June 21</p>
<p>Group Five:</p>
<p>In Nairobi:</p>
<p>Kenya 0 Cameroon 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>In Windhoek:</p>
<p>Namibia 1 Gabon 1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Namibia - Ruben van Wyk (86th)</p>
<p>Gabon - Pierre Aubame (19th penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Cameroon    3  1  2  0  4  0  4</p>
<p>    Kenya	 3  1  1  1  1  1  4</p>
<p>    Namibia     3  1  1  1  2  5  4</p>
<p>    Gabon	 3  0  2  1  1  2  2</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Kenya v Namibia, Nairobi, June 21</p>
<p>Cameroon v Gabon, Yaounde, June 22</p>
<p>Group Six:</p>
<p>In Dar-es-Salaam:</p>
<p>Tanzania 1 Liberia 1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Tanzania - Dua Said (75th)</p>
<p>Tanzania - Jonathan Sogbie (27th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>In Lome:</p>
<p>Togo 1 Zaire 1 (halftime 0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Togo - Kossi Noutsoudje (89th)</p>
<p>Zaire - Simba Ekanza (26th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Togo	3  2  1  0  5  3  7</p>
<p>    Zaire     3  1  2  0  3  2  5</p>
<p>    Liberia   3  0  2  1  2  3  2</p>
<p>    Tanzania  3  0  1  2  3  5  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Tanzania v Togo, Dar-es-Salaam, June 21</p>
<p>Liberia v Zaire, Monrovia, June 22</p>
<p>Group Seven:</p>
<p>In Blantyre:</p>
<p>Malawi 2 Mozambique 0 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: John Maduka (9th), Laurent Kamanga (60th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30,000</p>
<p>In Bellevue:</p>
<p>Mauritius 0 Zambia 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Zambia     3  2  1  0  3  0  7</p>
<p>    Malawi     3  2  0  1  4  3  6</p>
<p>    Mozambique 3  1  0  2  3  3  3</p>
<p>    Mauritius  3  0  1  2  1  5  1</p>
<p>Next matches:</p>
<p>Malawi v Mauritius, Blantyre, June 21</p>
<p>Mozambique v Zambia, Maputo, June 22</p>
<p>The top two teams in each group qualify for the finals in</p>
<p>Burkina Faso next February. Holders South Africa and the hosts</p>
<p>have already qualified.</p>
